    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Full suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nImplemented the soft-duplicate flag with minimal structural impact \u2014 added behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing existing methods or classes.\n\n**New file** \u2014 `PossibleDuplicate.java`: a single-purpose helper (mirroring the existing `ContactPreference` / `BulkSignupWarning` / `IdentityKey` pattern). Its `of(owner, repo)` returns the id of an *earlier* owner (lower id) sharing the same `lastName` and `postcode` but with a different normalized `telephone` \u2014 a soft-match that is by construction not a hard `IdentityKey` duplicate \u2014 or `null`.\n\n**Wiring** (3 lines each, no complexity added to existing methods):\n- `RespondWithOwner` (GET responder \u2014 the path the acceptance test asserts on) and `RespondWithOwnerCreated` (POST responder) each compute `possibleDuplicateOf` once, then set `possibleDuplicate` (`!= null`) and `possibleDuplicateOf`.\n\n**Schema** \u2014 `openapi.yml`: added the two read-only `Owner` properties so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes `possibleDuplicate` (boolean) and `possibleDuplicateOf` (int32).\n\nBecause the value is derived at response time from the repository (like the other derived fields), it's correct on both the create response and later GETs. Restricting the match to a lower-id (pre-existing) owner makes the result deterministic: the first owner reports `false`, the second reports `true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` = the first owner's id \u2014 exactly what `AcceptanceTest.coreFlagsPossibleDuplicate` checks.",
